# Windows shell commands

This project runs on Windows (PowerShell). Node.js installs three npm entry points: `npm`, `npm.cmd`, and `npm.ps1`.

In PowerShell, bare `npm` resolves to `npm.ps1`. When script execution is restricted, `npm` fails with:

> npm.ps1 cannot be loaded because running scripts is disabled on this system

## Required convention

On Windows, always run npm through the batch shim:

- `npm.cmd install`
- `npm.cmd run build`
- `npm.cmd test`

Do **not** use bash-style `&&` in PowerShell; chain with `;` instead:

```powershell
Set-Location "F:\path\to\repo"; npm.cmd run build; npm.cmd test
```

For project PowerShell scripts, use `scripts/invoke-npm.ps1` instead of bare `npm`.
